  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ved Prakash vs Municipal Corporation Of Delhi & Ors on 23 September, 2024 Author: Purushaindra Kumar Kaurav Bench: Purushaindra Kumar Kaurav $~96 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(C) 13302/2024 & Cm Appl. 55546/2024 Ved Prakash Through: Ms.Manpreet Kaur, Adv ve Municipal Corporation Of Delhi & Ors. .....Respo Through: Ms.Puja s.Kalra, Adv for Mr.Abhishek Khanna, Spc Mr.Kapil Yadav, Gp for Coram: HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE PURUSHAINDRA KUMAR KAURAV ORDER % 23.09.2024 CM APPL. 55547/2024 (Exemption) 1. Allowed, subject to all just exceptions.",
    "facts": "The instant petition has been filed seeking for the following reliefs:- (a) issue a writ of mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order or direction in the nature thereof, thereby directing the respondent No.1 to 4 to take immediate action against the Respondent No.5 to 7 for illegally encroaching on the public passage/road and running illegal eating house and food corner by the name of \"Sharma Corner\" & \"Veeru Fast Food & Chicken Corner\" from the property bearing No.4365, Gali No.58, Raigar Pura, Karol Bagh, New Delhi-110005; (b) pass any other or further order(s) as may this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case in favour of the petitioner and against the Respondent. 2. The Court takes note of the order dated 20.08.2024 in W.P.(C.) 11400/2024 titled as Sh. Nilabh Sharma v. Municipal Corporation of Delhi, wherein, the issue revolved around the causing of public nuisance due to the placement of dustbins near the petitioners house. This Court dismissed the petition while reserving the right in favour of the petitioner to avail the remedy under Section 152 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 [hereinafter referred as \"Sanhita\"].",
    "arguments": ""
  },
